@startuml
actor User
participant "React client" as UI
participant "FastAPI prediction route" as API
participant "ModelRegistry / ProductPipeline" as Pipe
participant "XGBoost model" as Model
participant "SHAPExplainer" as SHAP
participant "LIMEExplainer" as LIME
participant "Trust checks" as Trust
database "SQLAlchemy session" as DB
User -> UI : Submit application
UI -> API : POST /predict
API -> Pipe : select product, engineer, transform
Pipe -> Model : predict + predict_proba
Model --> Pipe : class + approval probability
Pipe -> SHAP : explain transformed row
SHAP --> Pipe : SHAP contributions
Pipe -> LIME : explain with seeded sampling
LIME --> Pipe : LIME contributions
Pipe -> Trust : compute four checks + weighted score
Trust --> API : trust evaluation
API -> DB : persist when available
API --> UI : prediction response
UI --> User : decision, explanations, metrics
note over API,Trust
Solvency is returned as metadata;
it does not override the model class.
end note
@enduml
